' Observed behavior: factory validates one prepared runtime before assembling the session.
' Design reason: expand and execute against that same runtime; persist only one ordinary user message.
' Java divergence: explicit structured input, fail closed, no added server path, ordinary domain persistence.
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
title Skill execution in the ordinary message lifecycle
participant "SkillCommandExecutionService\n(singleton, stateless)" as Skill
participant "RuntimeEventService\n(singleton, stateless)" as Events
participant "ContextFactory / Registry\n(singletons, operation lock)" as Runtime
participant "AgentSessionFactory\n(singleton)" as Factory
participant "PreparedAgentRuntime\n(one actual snapshot)" as Snapshot
database "Session Repository" as Repo
participant "Holder / Coordinator / Projector\n(active execution)" as Execution
Skill -> Skill: Normalize a defensive input copy
Skill -> Events: submitPreparedMessage(input function)
group Existing operation lock
Events -> Repo: Require idle and reconcile model
Events -> Runtime: Prepare context and acquire capacity
Runtime -> Factory: create(runtimeValidator)
Factory -> Snapshot: prepare once
Factory -> Skill: Callback with the actual snapshot
Skill -> Snapshot: requireBoundSkill and read content
Skill --> Runtime: One effective message
Runtime -> Runtime: Build UserMessage from that message
Factory --> Runtime: Session using the same snapshot
Runtime --> Events: Context with message and UserMessage
Events -> Repo: Accept ordinary user.message
Events -> Execution: Start the ordinary lifecycle
end
Execution -> Repo: Project existing domain events
Execution --> Skill: Ordinary SSE; detach does not abort
Repo -> Execution: Restore the saved message after restart
note over Runtime,Execution
Preparation failure releases capacity.
No command lifecycle or private skill snapshot is created.
end note
@enduml
